# Global shortcuts the Quattro shell registers (Hyprland only; on other compositors
# bind keys to the quattro-menu / quattro-shell commands instead, see the README), one per line: a menu
# route to toggle, a panel plugin to toggle, a volume or brightness key, or an
# argument-free IPC call as target.method. A binding written as o.bind(keys,
# description, { menu = "theme" }), { panel = "quattro.emojis" },
# { audio = "raise" }, { brightness = "raise" } or { ipc = "media.next" }
# dispatches the matching shortcut straight to the shell, with no process to
# spawn per keypress. Anything missing here still binds, through the
# quattro-menu, quattro-shell, quattro-audio-output-volume or
# quattro-brightness-display command instead.
menu root
menu apps
menu system
panel quattro.clipboard
panel quattro.emojis
panel quattro.audio
panel quattro.bluetooth
panel quattro.clock
panel quattro.elsewhen
panel quattro.network
panel quattro.power
audio raise
audio lower
audio mute-toggle
brightness raise
brightness lower
ipc media.playPause
ipc media.next
ipc media.previous
ipc notifications.act
ipc notifications.dismissOne
ipc notifications.dismissAll
ipc notifications.invokeLast
ipc notifications.showHistory
